## Goal
Address review feedback on the sync feature: make file copying safe against partial writes, and fix how iCloud paths are detected.

## Problems
The session slice was empty, so details come only from the commit message. The review evidently found two defects: a copy could leave a half-written destination file if interrupted, and iCloud detection matched too loosely because it lacked a path separator in the check.

## Decision
- Copy to a temporary file in the destination directory, then rename it over the target. A rename on the same filesystem is atomic, so readers see either the old file or the complete new one.
- Make iCloud detection require a path separator in the match, so only real iCloud directory components are recognised and not directory names that merely contain a similar substring.

